{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\nSummary:\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\n   The user (via an automated cobbler/stitch orchestrator) assigned task #5585 to implement `cmd/chroot/main.go` for the go-unix-utils project. The task requires implementing srd100-chroot requirements R1.1 (chroot execution with NEWROOT and COMMAND), R1.2 (--userspec=USER:GROUP flag), and R1.3 (--groups=G_LIST flag). The implementation must follow the project's execution constitution, go style guide, and shared protocols. No git commands should be run; only code writing and verification (go build, go vet) are expected.\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n   - `chroot(2)` system call via `syscall.Chroot` to change the root directory\n   - `syscall.Exec` to replace the process with COMMAND after chrooting\n   - `--userspec=USER:GROUP` flag to set UID/GID (names or numeric IDs)\n   - `--groups=G_LIST` flag to set supplementary groups (comma-separated names or GIDs)\n   - Default command is `${SHELL} -i` or `/bin/sh -i` if no COMMAND given\n   - Exit codes: 125 (chroot failure), 126 (command not invocable), 127 (command not found)\n   - SIGPIPE handling via `pkg/sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler()`\n   - Differential testing pattern against `gchroot` reference binary\n   - Non-goals: no `--skip-chdir`, no filesystem setup\n\n3. Files and Code Sections:\n   - `docs/specs/software-requirements/srd100-chroot.yaml` (READ)\n     - This is the SRD defining all requirements for the chroot utility\n     - R1.1: chroot(2) + execute COMMAND (or default shell)\n     - R1.2: --userspec=USER:GROUP sets UID/GID\n     - R1.3: --groups=G_LIST sets supplementary groups\n     - R2.1: Exit with COMMAND's exit status\n     - R2.2: Exit 125/126/127 for specific failure modes\n     - R2.3: SIGPIPE handling\n     - Non-goals: no --skip-chdir\n   \n   - `cmd/chroot/main.go` (TO CREATE)\n     - Must implement R1.1, R1.2, R1.3\n     - Must call `sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler()` at start of main\n     - Must use `syscall.Chroot` for the chroot(2) call\n     - Must use `os.Exit` for non-zero exit codes\n     - Must have copyright header\n\n   - `pkg/sys/sigpipe.go` (EXISTING, provided inline)\n     - Contains `InstallSIGPIPEHandler()` function\n     - ```go\n       func InstallSIGPIPEHandler() {\n           c := make(chan os.Signal, 1)\n           signal.Notify(c, syscall.SIGPIPE)\n           go func() {\n               <-c\n               os.Exit(0)\n           }()\n       }\n       ```\n\n4. Errors and fixes:\n   - No errors encountered yet. The SRD was successfully read and implementation has not begun.\n\n5. Problem Solving:\n   - Identified that the SRD file was not included in the inline project_context source_code section, so it needed to be read from disk.\n   - Successfully retrieved the full SRD with all requirement details needed for implementation.\n\n6. All user messages:\n   - First message: Massive task description with full project context, execution constitution, go style constitution, task requirements, constraints, SRD references, package contracts, shared protocols, and all inline source code for pkg/ packages. Task #5585 to implement cmd/chroot covering srd100-chroot R1.1-R1.3.\n   - Second message: \"CRITICAL: Respond with TEXT ONLY. Do NOT call any tools.\" — requesting a detailed summary of the conversation.\n\n7. Pending Tasks:\n   - Create `cmd/chroot/main.go` implementing:\n     - R1.1: chroot(2) + execute COMMAND or default shell\n     - R1.2: --userspec=USER:GROUP flag\n     - R1.3: --groups=G_LIST flag\n     - SIGPIPE handler installation\n     - Proper exit code handling (125/126/127)\n   - Verify compilation with `go build -o bin/chroot ./cmd/chroot/`\n   - Verify with `go vet ./cmd/chroot/`\n\n8. Current Work:\n   I had just finished reading the SRD at `docs/specs/software-requirements/srd100-chroot.yaml` and was about to implement `cmd/chroot/main.go`. The SRD revealed these key requirements:\n   - R1.1: \"Must call chroot(2) to change the root directory to NEWROOT, then execute COMMAND with any arguments. If no COMMAND is given, must execute ${SHELL} -i (default /bin/sh -i).\"\n   - R1.2: \"--userspec=USER:GROUP must set the UID and GID of the executed process. USER and GROUP may be names or numeric IDs.\"\n   - R1.3: \"--groups=G_LIST must set the supplementary groups of the executed process. G_LIST is a comma-separated list of group names or GIDs.\"\n   - Non-goals: no --skip-chdir\n   \n   No code has been written yet. The implementation approach involves:\n   - Parse flags (--userspec, --groups) and positional args (NEWROOT, COMMAND, ARGS...)\n   - Call syscall.Chroot(newroot) + os.Chdir(\"/\")\n   - Resolve user/group from names or numeric IDs\n   - Set supplementary groups via syscall.Setgroups\n   - Set GID via syscall.Setgid, UID via syscall.Setuid\n   - Exec the command via syscall.Exec (replacing the process)\n   - Handle error exit codes (125/126/127)\n\n9. Optional Next Step:\n   Write `cmd/chroot/main.go` implementing all three requirements (R1.1, R1.2, R1.3) with proper flag parsing, chroot execution, user/group specification, supplementary groups, SIGPIPE handling, and exit code management. Then verify with `go build -o bin/chroot ./cmd/chroot/` and `go vet ./cmd/chroot/`.\n   \n   The task description states: \"Complete all code changes before running `go build` or `go test`. Do not compile incrementally after each small edit.\"\n\nIf you need specific details from before compaction (like exact code snippets, error messages, or content you generated), read the full transcript at: /Users/pdiddy/.claude/projects/-private-var-folders-dl-cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn-T-go-unix-utils-worktrees-5585/3ad23a3c-ad01-42df-8317-965d63548b89.jsonl\nContinue the conversation from where it left off without asking the user any furth