{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01SX9Jt7NNznu3kTUYqiEnz2","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Excellent! Now I have all the information you requested. Let me provide a comprehensive summary of the patterns found.\n\n## Summary of Patterns Found\n\n### 1. Files Using syscall.Exec or Process Replacement\n\nTwo cmd implementations use `syscall.Exec` to replace the process:\n- **`cmd/nice/main.go`** (line 70): Uses `syscall.Exec(binary, argv, os.Environ())`\n- **`cmd/timeout/main.go`** (line 126): Uses `syscall.Exec(\"/bin/sh\", ...)` for signal re-raising\n\nThe other commands use `os/exec.Command` with `cmd.Run()` instead (env, nohup).\n\n### 2. Exit Code Patterns (125/126/127)\n\nAll implementations follow the same exit code convention:\n- **125**: Invalid argument, parsing error, or other command error\n- **126**: Permission denied / cannot execute (file exists but cannot run)\n- **127**: Command not found / No such file or directory\n\nExamples from the code:\n- **nice (line 66)**: Exit 127 when `exec.LookPath` fails\n- **nice (line 73)**: Exit 126 when `syscall.Exec` fails\n- **nice (line 37)**: Exit 125 for parsing errors\n- **timeout (line 46)**: Exit 127 for command not found\n- **timeout (line 49)**: Exit 126 for execution failures\n- **env (lines 48, 65, 66, 71)**: Exit 125 for argument errors; 127/126 for execution failures\n- **nohup (lines 25, 50, 88, 91)**: Exit 125 for operational errors; 127/126 for execution issues\n\n### 3. Flag Parsing Patterns\n\nAll implement **custom flag parsing** without using the standard `flag` package:\n\n- **nice**: Manual parsing with support for `-n N`, `--adjustment=N`, and GNU-style `-N` shortcuts (lines 77-163)\n- **timeout**: Sophisticated split between long flags and short flags with compound flag handling (lines 174-246)\n- **env**: Minimal custom parser checking for `-i`, `-0`, `-u` flags (lines 96-110)\n- **nohup**: No explicit flag parsing (accepts command + args)\n- **chown**: Custom long flag and short flag parsers (lines 412-461)\n\n### 4. SIGPIPE Handler\n\n**`pkg/sys/sigpipe.go`** (provided above) shows the standard pattern:\n```go\nfunc InstallSIGPIPEHandler() {\n    c := make(chan os.Signal, 1)\n    signal.Notify(c, syscall.SIGPIPE)\n    go func() {\n        <-c\n        os.Exit(0)\n    }()\n}\n```\n\nThis is called at the start of most commands (nice, timeout, env, nohup, chown) via `sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler()`.\n\n### Key Observations for Your Implementation\n\n1. **syscall.Exec pattern** (cmd/nice): When you need to completely replace the process, use `syscall.Exec(binary, argv, os.Environ())` after using `exec.LookPath()` to find the command.\n\n2. **os/exec.Command pattern** (cmd/env, cmd/nohup): When you need more control (signal handling, redirects, exit code inspection), use `exec.Command()` with `cmd.Run()` and inspect the returned `*exec.ExitError` for the actual exit code.\n\n3. **Error handling**: Always distinguish between command not found (127) and permission/execution errors (126) by checking for `exec.ErrNotFound` or `syscall.ENOENT`.\n\n4. **Always install SIGPIPE handler early** via `sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler()` to match GNU coreutils behavior (exits 0 on broken pipe)."}]}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"3ad23a3c-ad01-42df-8317-965d63548b89","uuid":"87f613bc-f74e-4163-ac02-feccfaf368a8","timestamp":"2026-05-27T14:38:44.304Z","tool_use_result":{"status":"completed","prompt":"In the repo at /private/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/5585, I need to see patterns from existing cmd/ implementations, specifically ones that:\n1. Use syscall.Exec to replace the process\n2. Use flag parsing with custom flags\n3. Handle exit codes 125/126/127\n\nLook at cmd/env/main.go, cmd/nice/main.go, cmd/nohup/main.go, or cmd/chown/main.go — whichever ones exist and have main.go files. Show me the full contents of 2-3 examples that use syscall.Exec or os.Exec patterns. Also check if there's a pkg/sys/sigpipe.go file and show its contents.","agentId":"acd170915b0103d28","agentType":"Explore","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Excellent! Now I have all the information you requested. Let me provide a comprehensive summary of the patterns found.\n\n## Summary of Patterns Found\n\n### 1. Files Using syscall.Exec or Process Replacement\n\nTwo cmd implementations use `syscall.Exec` to replace the process:\n- **`cmd/nice/main.go`** (line 70): Uses `syscall.Exec(binary, argv, os.Environ())`\n- **`cmd/timeout/main.go`** (line 126): Uses `syscall.Exec(\"/bin/sh\", ...)` for signal re-raising\n\nThe other commands use `os/exec.Command` with `cmd.Run()` instead (env, nohup).\n\n### 2. Exit Code Patterns (125/126/127)\n\nAll implementations follow the same exit code convention:\n- **125**: Invalid argument, parsing error, or other command error\n- **126**: Permission denied / cannot execute (file exists but cannot run)\n- **127**: Command not found / No such file or directory\n\nExamples from the code:\n- **nice (line 66)**: Exit 127 when `exec.LookPath` fails\n- **nice (line 73)**: Exit 126 when `syscall.Exec` fails\n- **nice (line 37)**: Exit 125 for parsing errors\n- **timeout (line 46)**: Exit 127 for command not found\n- **timeout (line 49)**: Exit 126 for execution failures\n- **env (lines 48, 65, 66, 71)**: Exit 125 for argument errors; 127/126 for execution failures\n- **nohup (lines 25, 50, 88, 91)**: Exit 125 for operational errors; 127/126 for execution issues\n\n### 3. Flag Parsing Patterns\n\nAll implement **custom flag parsing** without using the standard `flag` package:\n\n- **nice**: Manual parsing with support for `-n N`, `--adjustment=N`, and GNU-style `-N` shortcuts (lines 77-163)\n- **timeout**: Sophisticated split between long flags and short flags with compound flag handling (lines 174-246)\n- **env**: Minimal custom parser checking for `-i`, `-0`, `-u` flags (lines 96-110)\n- **nohup**: No explicit flag parsing (accepts command + args)\n- **chown**: Custom long flag and short flag parsers (lines 412-461)\n\n### 4. SIGPIPE Handler\n\n**`pkg/sys/sigpipe.go`** (provided above) shows the standard pattern:\n```go\nfunc InstallSIGPIPEHandler() {\n    c := make(chan os.Signal, 1)\n    signal.Notify(c, syscall.SIGPIPE)\n    go func() {\n        <-c\n        os.Exit(0)\n    }()\n}\n```\n\nThis is called at the start of most commands (nice, timeout, env, nohup, chown) via `sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler()`.\n\n### Key Observations for Your Implementation\n\n1. **syscall.Exec pattern** (cmd/nice): When you need to completely replace the process, use `syscall.Exec(binary, argv, os.Environ())` after using `exec.LookPath()` to find the command.\n\n2. **os/exec.Command pattern** (cmd/env, cmd/nohup): When you need more control (signal handling, redirects, exit code inspection), use `exec.Command()` with `cmd.Run()` and inspect the returned `*exec.ExitError` for the actual exit code.\n\n3. **Error handling**: Always distinguish between command not found (127) and permission/execution errors (126) by checking for `exec.ErrNotFound` or `syscall.ENOENT`.\n\n4. **Always install SIGPIPE handler early** via `sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler()` to match GNU coreutils behavior (exits 0 on broken pipe)."}],"totalDurationMs":25936,"totalTokens":35478,"totalToolUseCount":11,"usage":{"input_tokens":5,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1437,"cache_read_input_tokens":33097,"output_tokens":939,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1437},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":5,"output_tokens":939,"cache_read_input_tokens":33097,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1437,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1437,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"toolStats":{"readCount":7,"searchCount":1,"bashCount":3,"editFileCount":0,"linesAdded":0,"linesRemoved":0,"